00:00:00,100 --> 00:00:03,890
Which drone's position can you trust? Three simulated drones. One person decides.

2
00:00:03,890 --> 00:00:10,338
TRUSTED. All three report a trusted position.

3
00:00:10,338 --> 00:00:14,389
DO NOT TRUST. uav2's position froze. The system says why.

4
00:00:14,389 --> 00:00:18,210
Frozen position flagged in 3.0 to 4.5 s, 7 simulation runs.

5
00:00:18,210 --> 00:00:22,301
It recommends landing uav2. It cannot act alone.

6
00:00:22,301 --> 00:00:27,917
Nothing moves until a person approves.

7
00:00:27,917 --> 00:00:32,157
Approved by Duty operator. Recorded in the audit log.

8
00:00:32,157 --> 00:00:37,609
Nothing moves until a person approves. What this does not show: real hardware or radio interference, and a usability result. Simulation only. Not flight-tested. telschow.github.io/nav-trust-c2
